```cpp
static void MaybeAppendWithLength(State *state, const char * const str, ssize_t length) {
  if (state->append && length > 0) {
    if (str[0] == '<' && state->out_begin < state->out_cur  &&
        state->out_cur[-1] == '<') {
      Append(state, " ", 1);
    }
    if (IsAlpha(str[0]) || str[0] == '_') {
      state->prev_name = state->out_cur;
      state->prev_name_length = length;
    }
    Append(state, str, length);
  }
}
```

If `length > 0` and `str[0]` is read. `str` is `state->mangled_cur`. If `mangled_cur` points to the null terminator at Buffer[Size], then `str[0]` = 0, which is fine. But if `mangled_cur` points past the buffer...

